<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Xuge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">707 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Xuge was fought in 707 BCE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-huan-of-zhou">King Huan of Zhou</a>, with contingents from Chen, Cai and Wey, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-zhuang-of-zheng">Duke Zhuang of Zheng</a>. Zheng's army routed the royal forces, and an archer wounded the king in the shoulder. The defeat of the king by one of his own lords marked the decline of Zhou royal power early in the Spring and Autumn period.</p></div>
